[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Probe.cs" id="1_probe"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Marker.cs" id="2_marker"]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; godot-abi-grid — AUTHORED GROUND TRUTH (docs/analysis.md §8.9)
;
; Every number in this file is load-bearing. Read §8.9 before changing any of
; them, then re-run `node gen-expected.mjs`.
;
;  * Sizes are NON-ROUND and mutually distinct. §12.5 probe 15 got four
;    candidate offsets for a 200x50 control because round numbers recur
;    throughout memory. 613x227 / 409x151 / 887x313 make a single scan
;    near-unique and a two-control intersection certainly unique.
;  * EXACTLY ONE size is duplicated on purpose (409x151 on AlphaLeaf and on
;    GammaNest) to prove the calibrator does not collapse distinct nodes.
;  * Nesting is 7 levels deep with sibling counts 2/3/4/3/2/3 — uneven, so the
;    intrusive child-list walk and the parent pointer are both exercised.
;  * ZetaLabelUnicode / ZetaRich carry non-ASCII text including an astral
;    codepoint (U+1D11E). §4.6: scry truncates char32_t -> byte. The harness
;    MUST fail if our decoder does the same.
;  * THE TWO-INSTANCE RULE. Every property the calibrator has to DISCRIMINATE
;    must be backed by at least two nodes. The calibrator publishes an offset
;    only when decode-set ⊆ property-set with a non-empty decode-set; over a
;    ONE-element set that is arithmetically vacuous — any field of the right
;    shape on that one node satisfies it — so the calibrator correctly withholds
;    rather than publish on no evidence, and the field goes unmeasured forever.
;    That is not hypothetical: Label had two instances and derived cleanly on
;    23/24 cell-runs, while RichTextLabel had one and richTextLabel.text was
;    NEVER derived, on any cell, in eight grid series.
;
;    The scene had four such one-element sets. All four are now doubled:
;      RichTextLabel      ZetaRich        + OmegaRich    (text offset)
;      scripted node      RootHarness     + OmegaMarker  (node.scriptInstance,
;                                                         and the whole bridge)
;      visible = false    HiddenTwin      + OmegaHidden  (canvasItem.visible)
;      non-zero anchors   AnchoredWide    + OmegaAnchored (Data.anchor vs
;                                                          Data.offset)
;    gen-expected.mjs now FAILS if any of them drops back to one, so the next
;    one of these cannot be discovered the way the first four were.
;
;    Doubling a sample is not enough on its own: the second instance must be
;    able to DISAGREE with the first, or two nodes are one measurement made
;    twice. So each pair differs in kind, not just in address — see the note on
;    each node below.
;  * VisibleTwin / HiddenTwin are the visible-flag pair.
;  * AnchoredWide has non-zero anchors, so its position/size are computed from
;    the parent rect rather than being the raw offsets — this is the shape that
;    produced StS2's BgContainer offset[-960,-516,1600,684] in §4.6.
;  * clip_text on the Labels stops Label::get_minimum_size() from overriding
;    the authored size.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

[node name="RootHarness" type="Control"]
